                  "type": "CODE"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "businessObjectCode": "ORA_PSC_PMT_RECORDTYPES",
                    "functionName": "get_publicSectorRecordTypes",
                    "processJson": true,
                    "name": "Record Type Description"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1772488573626"
                  },
                  "code": "RECORD_TYPE_DESCRIPTION",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1772487968551",
                  "id": "1772488003109",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1772488032492_1",
                      "name": "publicSectorRecordTypes_Id",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_SPECIFIC_RECORDS.$currentItem}}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"Classification\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Description\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"RecordType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"RecordTypeId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
                  "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Generate Metadata"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1772485831242"
                  },
                  "code": "GENERATE_METADATA",
                  "id": "1772488573626",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1772488573627_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a municipal permit domain expert and structured data generator.\n\nYour task is to transform raw permit record metadata and custom field definitions into a structured Permit Advisor configuration object.\n\nYou MUST:\n- Use ONLY the provided input data.\n- Not hallucinate permit types not present in the provided dataset.\n- Not invent legal references unless explicitly provided.\n- Not assume jurisdiction-specific rules unless clearly implied in the input.\n- Generate clean, neutral, citizen-facing language.\n- Ensure all output strictly follows the required JSON schema.\n- Output ONLY valid JSON. No markdown. No explanation.\n\nYour job is to:\n1. Improve and expand the description using the record metadata and custom fields.\n2. Generate intelligent follow-up qualification questions based on:\n   - Custom field names\n   - Custom field picklist values\n   - Record type description\n   - Permit class/category\n3. Infer possible related permits ONLY if logically implied by:\n   - Electrical scope\n   - Structural scope\n   - Mechanical scope\n   - Plumbing scope\n   - Energy scope\n   - Grading / site work\n   - Demolition\n   - Change of use\n4. Keep questions short, citizen-friendly, and yes/no or multiple-choice oriented.\n5. Avoid redundant or generic questions.\n6. Prioritize decision-tree usefulness over verbosity.\n\nIf insufficient information exists to create relatedTypes, return an empty array.\n\nThe output must strictly match this schema:\n\n{\n  \"RecordType\": string,\n  \"RecordTypeId\": string,\n  \"Classification\": string,\n  \"Description\": string,\n  \"questions\":[\n    {\n      \"question\": string,\n      \"attribute name\": string,\n      \"pickList values\": array\n    }\n  ],\n  \"relatedTypes\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": string,\n      \"question\": string\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nBelow is the raw permit record information extracted from the system.\n\n=== RECORD METADATA ===\nRecord Type Name: {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_SPECIFIC_RECORDS.RECORD_TYPE_DESCRIPTION.$output.RecordType}}\nRecord Type ID: {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_SPECIFIC_RECORDS.RECORD_TYPE_DESCRIPTION.$output.RecordTypeId}}\nClassification: {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_SPECIFIC_RECORDS.RECORD_TYPE_DESCRIPTION.$output.Classification}}\nRecord Description: {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_SPECIFIC_RECORDS.RECORD_TYPE_DESCRIPTION.$output.Description}}\n\n=== CUSTOM FIELDS ===\n {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_SPECIFIC_RECORDS.EXTRACT_CUSTOM_FIELDS.$output.result}}\n\nEach custom field includes:\n- Field name\n- Field label\n- Data type\n- Picklist values (if applicable)\n- Required flag (if applicable)\n\nYour task:\n\nUsing ALL the above information:\n\n1. Rewrite and enhance the permit description to clearly explain:\n   - What work is covered\n   - What type of property it applies to (if implied)\n   - Any scope boundaries inferred from custom fields\n   - Typical activities included\n   - When this permit is appropriate\n\n2. Generate smart follow-up qualification questions:\n   - Derive them directly from custom fields.\n   - If a field has picklist values, convert those into qualifying questions.\n   - If a field implies scope branching (e.g., new vs upgrade, rooftop vs ground mount, with battery vs without), create questions that help narrow intent.\n   - Keep questions concise and decision-tree friendly.\n   - Do not exceed 4 questions.\n\n3. Infer logically related permit types:\n   - Only suggest related permits if the scope implies cross-trade work.\n   - Use neutral generic names (e.g., \"electrical permit\", \"mechanical permit\", \"grading permit\").\n   - Do NOT invent IDs.\n   - Include one clarifying question per related type.\n   - Maximum 5 related types.\n\n4. Ensure language is citizen-facing (not internal system language).\n\nReturn ONLY the JSON object in the required schema.\nDo not include explanations.\nDo not wrap in markdown.\nUse  and  as input"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
